  "description": "Names, generic feature types and geometries of seafloor features (seamounts, canyons, banks, ridges, basins, guyots, fracture zones, trenches ...) approved by the IHO-IOC GEBCO Sub-Committee on Undersea Feature Names (SCUFN), from the NOAA NCEI / IHO DCDB Undersea_Features feature service. The service has three layers, one per geometry type (2,632 points, 1,128 lines, 1,652 polygons), all kept here with the per-row `geom_type` (MultiPoint, MultiLineString or MultiPolygon) and `component` (point, line, polygon). `FEATURE_ID`, the gazetteer's permanent feature number, is the id: a feature that the service serves as both a point and an extent (101 do) keeps `GEBCO:<FEATURE_ID>` on its polygon (else line) and gets `:point` or `:line` on the other rows. Built by build.py from 3 source layer(s).",
